First mooted on Lojban list:

  So I think "experience of having legs" is NOT "li'i ce'u se tuple" but
  rather "li'i le se NO'AU se tuple", where NO'AU = next outer phrase
  (regardless of whether it is a bridi) = a sibling of NO'A.

--((And))

(sorry, I can't resist thinking that ''no'au'' is something like a strong form of ''ka'enai'' or ''.e'enai''... zo'o)
*''ka'enai'' : ''no how''? and ''.e'enai'' = what? ''.e'e'' = ''knowhow''?
**Also "no how", just a different sense thereof.  I didn't even think of "knowhow."
